caption: Two pictures showing a real torus, that is homeomorphic to the elliptic curve. The left picture presents the torus as \(\mathbb{R}^{2} / \mathbb{Z}^{2}\). The right one is the familiar figure we know from topology. The two thickened circles, on both pictures, correspond to the real part of the curve.
